<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41296" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτέλλω</span></b>  (B), 
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rise,</i> of
			stars, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πληϊάδων.. ἐπιτελλομενάων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					383
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρκτοῦρος..
			ἐπιτέλλεται</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				567
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠελίοιο νέον -ομένοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					371
				</span></i>
			 : so intr. in 
				Act.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Int.</u>
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				345b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				9.15.9
			</span></i>, etc. : the aor.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπλόμενος</span> belongs as much to
			this verb as to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπέλομαι</span> (q.v.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. of love, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡραῖος καὶ Ἔρως ἐπιτέλλεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1275
				</span></i>
			. (Hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπολή</span> and (later)
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτολή.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
